Draw the **Lattice inserter**, a 12-frame **sprite sheet** of an animated
swing-arm machine, using only the drawing tool.

The inserter is a renderer sprite for **Lattice**, a factory simulation rendered
in **Factorio's high-angle, pseudo-3D style** — you are looking *down* on the
machine, consistent with the assembler, **not** drawing a side elevation. You are
drawing one inserter mounted on the centre tile, viewed in its canonical
orientation: it **picks an item up from the tile on its left**, swings the item in
an arc **across the floor**, and **drops it on the tile to its right**. Across the
twelve frames the arm sweeps from left to right carrying the item, then swings back
empty, so the animation loops seamlessly. The pivot base sits at the centre of the
frame and the arm's raised height reads from shading and a contact shadow on the
floor, not from the arm climbing up the screen. The renderer rotates this one
sprite for the other facings, so you draw this one orientation only. The brief's
**The look** section is the thing to get right.

## How drawing works

The only way to make a mark is the `draw-sheet` binary already on your `PATH`. You
build the sheet by calling it **one operation at a time**, each targeting a frame
with `--frame <index>`. The ordered operations you issue are recorded to a per-frame
action log, and that log is your submission.

Each frame is its **own separate 64×64 image**. After each call the binary
re-renders that frame to `frames/<index>.png` and appends the operation to that
frame's log. Blank starting frames and empty logs are already in place at
`{{workspace}}`.

Each operation is an ordinary subcommand with flags, naming its frame:

```
draw-sheet fill-rect --frame 0 --x 24 --y 26 --width 16 --height 12 --color "#4d5a64"
```

Run `draw-sheet --help` to list every operation and `draw-sheet <operation>
--help` for one operation's exact flags — that help text is the authoritative
contract. **Read `frames/<index>.png` after your calls** to see your progress and
decide what to do next.

## What to read first

The full specification is in the `specs/` directory at `{{workspace}}`, already
present in your project. Read all of it before you start, and produce an
implementation that matches the specification exactly.

## What to deliver

Build the inserter sprite sheet up operation by operation until each
`frames/<index>.png` matches the brief: a fixed grey-blue base with an amber swing
arm and claw, sweeping a held steel plate in an arc from the left pickup to the
right drop over frames 0→5 and swinging back empty over frames 6→11, so the loop
reads as one continuous pickup-swing-drop-return cycle. When you are satisfied,
stop: the recorded per-frame action logs are your finished submission.
